{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"1f013f6426b27f8cb555c22229b6c039f0c3bf25e128f377b49ae37cdbaeeacb","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconcile bridge — outbound comment sync","key_entities":["comment_ids","RECONCILER_MARKER","outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body","_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX","adapters/jira/comment_limits.py","REB-1861","run 32403944666","712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e","cleanup.py","--include-truncated"],"problem_keywords":["duplicate comments","jira cleanup","comment dedup","reconciler bug","5000 comment cap"],"propositions":["The Jira reconcile bridge re-posted the same comments repeatedly because the primary comment-id dedup map was inert, causing 30,847 duplicate bot-authored comments across 30 issues (REB-1861 reached the 5000-comment hard cap).","A T4 safety-gated cleanup removed 29,931 duplicates by keeping the oldest copy per distinct normalized body, with pre-deletion full backups, dry run, canary verification, and independent post-deletion verification confirming zero missing distinct bodies.","Three issues (REB-1567, REB-1931, REB-2605) carry 836 additional comments without the reconciler marker because outbound truncation at 32767 chars cut off the marker paragraph; these were deliberately held for phase 2 pending operator review.","The reconcile-bridge workflow remains paused and was not re-enabled by this ticket; the underlying defect (irongrey-chubby-oxpecker) was fixed separately."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787881042398664001,"uuid":"7ed7bf6f-283e-4dd8-b524-4c5665c46143"}